course: dictionary
lesson: 12234
title: Thinking before you act
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Consideration is a noun with a few meanings that link together. It can mean careful thought before you decide something: «After much consideration, Mia chose the blue bike.»
explain: It can also mean kindness and thought for other people's feelings and needs: «Please show consideration for others when you share the swings.» The clue is the word others, so this meaning is about how people feel.
explain: Read the words around it to find the meaning. «Cost is an important consideration when we plan the school trip.» Cost is something we must think about before we decide, so here consideration means a thing to think about. Swap in "thing to think about" and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Consideration is a noun. Its plural is considerations.
fact: «Consideration» can mean careful thought before deciding.
fact: «Consideration» can mean kindness and thought for other people's feelings and needs.
fact: «Consideration» can mean something you must think about when you decide.
fact: In a formal sense, consideration means payment for something.
fact: Useful phrases: take into consideration, under consideration, out of consideration for, give it careful consideration.
exercise: «After much consideration, Ava chose the red paint.» What does consideration mean here? | A loud argument | Kindness for other people | Something to paint with | *Careful thought before deciding
exercise: «Please show consideration for others at lunch.» What does consideration mean here? | A plan for the day | Careful thought about the weather | Money paid for the lunch | *Kindness and thought for other people's feelings
exercise: «Cost is an important consideration when we plan a trip.» What does consideration mean here? | A payment we have already made | A map of the route | Kindness to the driver | *Something to think about before deciding
test: The plan is «under consideration» by the teachers. What does under consideration mean? | Shouted out loudly | Lost in the post | *Being thought about right now | Finished and never to be changed
test: What is the plural of consideration? | Considerate | *Considerations | Considers | Considerers
exam: Which sentence uses consideration to mean kindness? | «The sky was grey and wet all day.» | «We made a long list of things to pack for the trip.» | «The trip was under consideration for next term.» | *«Lia let her little brother go first, out of consideration for him.»
